component JuxtParen
export Executable

(*) Probe 5: the specification writes REM's defining property as
(*) "m REM n = m - n(m DIV n)" (basic-lib/basic-integers.tex:481), with the
(*) product spelled as a juxtaposition of a variable and a parenthesised
(*) expression.  library_tests/Integer3.fss:67 juxtaposes two variables
(*) ("seven five"), but nothing in the corpus juxtaposes a variable with a
(*) parenthesised expression, and "b (e)" is also the spelling of a function
(*) call.  This probe decides whether the body can be written in the
(*) specification's spelling or has to use DOT, which on ZZ32 is the same
(*) native (jIntOverflowingMul, CompilerBuiltin.fss:637 and :652).

run(): () = do
    a: ZZ32 = 8
    b: ZZ32 = 3
    println("a - b (a DIV b) = " || (a - b (a DIV b)).asString)
    println("a - (b DOT (a DIV b)) = " || (a - (b DOT (a DIV b))).asString)
  end
end
